[
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsMulTorsionFree#doc\">docs#IsMulTorsionFree</a> states that exponentiation by <code>n</code> on <code>G</code> is injective for all positive <code>n</code>. But for infinite nonabelian groups this is not necessarily equivalent to \"G has no torsion elements\" (for positive <code>n</code>, if <code>g ^ n = 1</code> then <code>g = 1</code>). Does this mean that our definition of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsMulTorsionFree#doc\">docs#IsMulTorsionFree</a> is wrong? Or are both notions worth studying? (in which case how should they be named?)</p>",
        "id": 614317763,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1785763497
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(for an example, take the infinite group with presentation <code>x ^ 2 = y ^ 2</code>, so that <code>x</code> and <code>y</code> don't have finite order but square to the same value)</p>",
        "id": 614317906,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1785763539
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Relevant discussion <a href=\"https://mathoverflow.net/q/106193/593996\">https://mathoverflow.net/q/106193/593996</a></p>",
        "id": 614319086,
        "sender_full_name": "Yakov Pechersky",
        "timestamp": 1785763886
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think your suggestion is close to a revert of <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/22962\">#22962</a>?</p>",
        "id": 614345977,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1785770941
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"387244\">@Yaël Dillies</span>, do you have thoughts on this?</p>",
        "id": 614350547,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1785772118
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok, I finally had a chance to look this over. <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"387244\">@Yaël Dillies</span> claims in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/22962\">#22962</a> that <code>∀ a : α, n • a = 0 → a = 0</code> is the incorrect definition of torsion free for additive monoids. But for nonabelian infinite groups like <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟨</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∣</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\langle x,y\\mid x^2=y^2\\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">⟨</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">⟩</span></span></span></span>, I think it would be entirely correct to call this group torsion-free despite it only satisfying <code>∀ a : α, n • a = 0 → a = 0</code>.</p>",
        "id": 614363099,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1785776305
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So from the perspective of group theory, I think we definitely want <code>∀ g : G, g ^ n = 1 → g = 1</code> as a definition in mathlib.</p>",
        "id": 614363197,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1785776337
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Perhaps we also want the injectivity version as well, but this is less clear to me.</p>",
        "id": 614363502,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1785776446
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There's also the option of using <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"762865\">@Pace Nielsen</span>'s definition in the Mathoverflow question (for groups, it is implied by the weaker <code>∀ g : G, g ^ n = 1 → g = 1</code> since if <code>s</code> and <code>t</code> commute with <code>s ^ n = t ^ n</code>, then <code>(s / t) ^ n = 1</code> so <code>s = t</code>.</p>",
        "id": 614363931,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1785776603
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>btw the implication is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsMulTorsionFree.pow_right_injective#doc\">docs#IsMulTorsionFree.pow_right_injective</a></p>",
        "id": 614364574,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1785776852
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"253861\">Thomas Browning</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Definition.20of.20.60IsMulTorsionFree.60/near/614317763\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>(in which case how should they be named?)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>How about</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HasUniqueRoots</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Monoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">npow_const_injective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⦃</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">⦄</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Injective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- or maybe just `IsStronglyMulTorsionFree`</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsMulTorsionFree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Monoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">const_npow_injective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⦃</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">⦄</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Injective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 614367614,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1785778017
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've started playing around with Pace Nielsen's definition in the Mathoverflow question, and it's looking promising. Basically, it seems to give a nice reconciliation of the group-theory definition and the commutative semigroup definition. Here's the PR: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42407\">#42407</a></p>",
        "id": 614395128,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1785785227
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For curiosity, what use case did this come up in?</p>",
        "id": 614401685,
        "sender_full_name": "Yakov Pechersky",
        "timestamp": 1785787975
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>A recent Annals paper claiming that a certain nomabelian group was torsion-free</p>",
        "id": 614405031,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1785789112
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And we got rather surprised when Claude told us that the theorem was false</p>",
        "id": 614405117,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1785789130
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(because the current definition of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsMulTorsionFree#doc\">docs#IsMulTorsionFree</a> isn't the usual group-theoretic definition that we were expecting)</p>",
        "id": 614406505,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1785789603
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I do not mind what the definition is so long as you preserve my application to <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsAffineMonoid#doc\">docs#IsAffineMonoid</a>. See <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Affine_monoid\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Affine_monoid</a> for my reference here, which uses the current definition of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsMulTorsionFree#doc\">docs#IsMulTorsionFree</a>.</p>",
        "id": 614466636,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1785824627
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The \"real\" application (ie an application that's not just about setting up definitions but actually using them) is part of the second phase of the Toric project and hasn't been written yet.</p>",
        "id": 614467052,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1785824848
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That Wikipedia page says \"affine monoids are torsion free\" and the link on \"torsion free\" links to a wikpiedia page in differential geometry about connections. This makes me wonder whether whoever (or whatever) wrote that page didn't really know what they were talking about. I am not sure that \"torsion free\" means what mathlib currently says it means and I think this source (which only applies in the abelian case) is dubious.</p>",
        "id": 614489414,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1785833277
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"387244\">Yaël Dillies</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Definition.20of.20.60IsMulTorsionFree.60/near/614466636\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I do not mind what the definition is so long as you preserve my application to <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsAffineMonoid#doc\">docs#IsAffineMonoid</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Ah, good. Those monoids are commutative, and I'm only changing the definition in the non-commutative case (really does seem like the commutative semigroup people and the group theorists just have different definitions that agree on the overlap and can be reconciled by the definition in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42407\">#42407</a>).</p>",
        "id": 614492681,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Browning",
        "timestamp": 1785834364
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have started a discussion on Wikipedia: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Affine_monoid#c-Yaël_Dillies-20260804105000-Definition_of_torsion-free_monoids\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Affine_monoid#c-Yaël_Dillies-20260804105000-Definition_of_torsion-free_monoids</a></p>",
        "id": 614510294,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1785840686
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>There are (at least) three candidate definitions</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>FWIW there's also TF2 from the MO post, and the weakest definition could be strengthened to support semigroups, giving a total of 5 different linearly ordered definitions:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Commute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The first one is our current <code>IsMulTorsionFree</code>, the last one is its previous incarnation <code>Monoid.IsTorsionFree</code>, and the second one is the proposed new definition.</p>\n<p>Commutativity merges the first two, cancellative multiplication merges the last three, and <code>Group</code> merges the last four.</p>\n<p>I don't know which of these are actually useful in theorems, but <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/24311/files#diff-287f2d2144c26e0a7d5c92d6c66059de2e50bb3fec1b9e9589ad0178a6f821da\">evidently</a> we have a theorem about <code>Group</code>s which doesn't require the full strength of the first definition.</p>\n<p>(there's also <code>∀ a, ∀ m n : ℕ+, m ≠ n → a ^ m = a ^ n → a = 1</code> but it doesn't support semigroups and it makes the implication order non-linear; it implies the 3rd property and is incomparable with the first two)</p>",
        "id": 614792868,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1785943876
    }
]